t\nIt started. It's listening on 5173 (Vite default). I should also check if the backend started on 3000.\n\nLet's check the logs.\n\n<channel|><|tool_call>call:read_file{path:<|\"|>.agent_logs/cmd_out_1791403977.log<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:read_file{value:<|\"|>npm notice run realtime-message-board@1.0.0 dev\nnpm notice run concurrently \"npm run dev --prefix backend\" \"npm run dev --prefix frontend\"\n[1] npm notice run frontend@1.0.0 dev\n[1] npm notice run vite\n[0] npm notice run backend@1.0.0 dev\n[0] npm notice run node server.js\n[0] /tmp/runs/smokes/gemma-q4/message-board/interactive/runs/301/app/backend/server.js:13\n[0] const db = new PGLite('./pgdata');\n[0]            ^\n[0] \n[0] TypeError: PGLite is not a constructor\n[0]     at Object.<anonymous> (/tmp/runs/smokes/gemma-q4/message-board/interactive/runs/301/app/backend/server.js:13:12)\n[0]     at Module._compile (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1929:14)\n[0]     at Object..js (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:2060:10)\n[0]     at Module.load (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1651:32)\n[0]     at Module._load (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1443:12)\n[0]     at wrapModuleLoad (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:261:19)\n[0]     at Module.executeUserEntryPoint [as runMain] (node:internal/modules/run_main:154:5)\n[0]     at node:internal/main/run_main_module:33:47\n[0] \n[0] Node.js v24.21.0\n[0] npm run dev --prefix backend exited with code 1\n[1] \n[1]   VITE v5.4.21  ready in 101 ms\n[1] \n[1]   ➜  Local:   http://localhost:5173/\n[1]   ➜  Network: use --host to expose\n<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|channel>thought\nThe backend failed with `TypeError: PGLite is not a constructor`.\nThis is because I imported `PGLite` from `@electric-sql/pglite` using `const { PGLite } = require('@electric-sql/pglite');`.\n\nIn recent versions of `@electric-sql/pglite`, the export might be different. Let me check how to import it in CommonJS.\n\nAccording to PGLite documentation, it should be `import 